title: Excessive Militarization of the the Banners
subtitle: Many argue that its militarization is no longer necessary now that we have established dominance over the streets.
view-if: banner_militancy >= 0.15 and democracy_paramilitary_highest and year >= 1931 and not banner_massive
new-page: true
tags: event
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/reichsbanner_flag.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= Excessive Militarization of the the Banners

The argument that the militarization of the the Banners is necessary to defend against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> no longer holds, given our dominance of the streets. With the threat now eliminated, the propertied parties fear it may instead function as a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> militia.

[? if not banner_exit: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] [? if not lvp_formed:and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>&nbsp;?][? if not lvp_leave_banner and lvp_formed:and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>&nbsp;?]have threatened drastic consequences if the the Banners isn't disarmed.?]
[? if banner_exit and not concord_formed: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?][? if not lvp_formed: and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if not lvp_leave_banner and lvp_formed: and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] have condemned the organization as nothing more than a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> militia and have abandoned their strong opposition to the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span>.?][? if (banner_exit or concord_leave_banner) and concord_formed: The <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span> [? if not lvp_formed: and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if not lvp_leave_banner and lvp_formed: and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] have condemned the organization as nothing more than a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> militia and are getting noticeably friendly with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span>.?]

If no action is taken, we risk permanently alienating the propertied parties.

- @let_go: Refuse to take any action, keeping the the Banners the way it is.
- @lower_militancy: We must lower the the Banners's militancy.

@let_go
subtitle: The the Banners is still needed, as the police cannot be trusted to do their job. [? if president == "DuFour" and marcher_in_government: DuFour has threatened to sack our government if no action is taken. ?][? if marcher_in_government and not in_left_front and not in_marcher_majority: Our coalition partners will call a vote of no confidence. ?] The propertied parties will be forever antagonistic.
unavailable-subtitle: The reformist wing of the party is able to dissuade the party from endorsing this option.
choose-if: left_strength + knight_strength >= reformist_strength
on-arrival: banner_strength *= 0.8; unionist_relation -= 20; ddp_relation -= 20; lvp_relation -= 20; banner_exit = 1; left_strength += 10*(1-dissent); knight_strength += 20*(1-dissent); ddp_right += 8; lvp_right += 10; gold_right += 10; ddp_cohesion -= 5; pro_republic -= 10; coalition_dissent += 5; banner_massive = 1; dufour_angry += 100

We must not let our guard down; the the Banners must remain militarized. Whether they like it or not, paramilitaries are here to stay.

Unfortunately, the propertied parties[? if president == "DuFour":, and especially President DuFour?] now plainly see the the Banners for what it is: our <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> militia. Non-<span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> members of the paramilitary leave en masse, and the political establishment will be forever antagonistic to us.

@lower_militancy
subtitle: The necessity for paramilitaries is over; we can now let the Heartland police do its job.
on-arrival: banner_militancy *= 0.5

Bowing to the other parties' demands, we reduce the the Banners's military training, thus inducing them to stay.
